# Source map for {{name}}

Every directive in SKILL.md must have a row. A directive is only as authoritative as its locator.

| Directive | Source locator | Status | Note |
|---|---|---|---|
| D-01 | TODO(chapter, section, page or line of the source) | AUTHOR-ADDITION | TODO |

Status values:

- `SOURCE-CLAIM`: the source says this. The locator points at where.
- `AUTHOR-ADDITION`: the skill author added this (a workflow step, a guard). It is not the source's claim and must not be presented as one.
- `UNSOURCED`: no locator yet. Release requires `ack:` from the user in the note.
